ive","html_url":"https://github.com/cryoboltinteractive","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cryoboltinteractive/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cryoboltinteractive/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cryoboltinteractive/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cryoboltinteractive/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cryoboltinteractive/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cryoboltinteractive/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cryoboltinteractive/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cryoboltinteractive/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cryoboltinteractive/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-27T18:52:25Z","updated_at":"2024-10-27T18:52:25Z","body":"![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ef4034f1-aa84-444d-9872-234648098630)\r\n\r\nOpened the file in blender, seems like this is a very weird way of dealing with alpha. Usually you'd have the lid as a separate object and the liquid also as a separate object. Even blender will struggle to achieve a desired look.\r\nThere will be Z fighting as Alpha is calculated per face and not on UV pixels. and this is true for any 3D Program.\r\nThe standard material will not work for this model and texture, unless you separate out the Lid, Liquid and the Jug.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2440135493/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2440487663","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98377#issuecomment-2440487663","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/